			<div class="content" id="post-content-4833510">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> Tale</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Action/Adventure, maybe a touch of horror</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Normal story stuff</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The UIU encounters The Aristocrats (SCP 3288)</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> When Emperor Maximilian I went to Mexico to take the throne, whether knowingly or not, a collection of his &quot;cousins&quot; came with him. While they've managed to fly relatively below the radar until now, a series of disappearances and particularly gruesome recovered bodies along the US/Mexico border have sparked interest.</p>
<p>When a cell phone is recovered with one of the bodies, and holds a picture of what is deemed a &quot;malformed humanoid&quot; a detachment from the UIU is sent to take over the investigation, as it still seems plausible that this could be connected to a relatively mundane criminal or group that has something &quot;mildly&quot; extraordinary at their disposal.</p>
<p>The investigation eventually carries the group into discovering the lair employed by this specific family. They would prefer to requisition back up of course, but something, perhaps the presence of still live victims, forces their hand to move in ahead of schedule&#8230; Or, maybe they do get proper &quot;prep time&quot; to even the odds.</p>
<p>Either way, we get the climactic battle between the two groups, and maybe implications that this isn't the only such branch out there. They equate power with status, perhaps the UIU has only encountered a &quot;minor&quot; baron?</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> An old fashioned &quot;monster battle&quot; adventure story with the Bureau. Can they eke out a win?</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Phone posted, so this is especially truncated.</p>

