			<div class="content" id="post-content-4836174">
									

<p>I'd love to see more FBI stories that manage to not get bogged down in X-files revanchism.</p>
<p>The key is to develop your main characters in a way that isn't a Mulder and Scully rehash.</p>
<p>So I'll give you the character workshopping template questions:</p>
<p>How are the relations between the characters? Do they like each other?</p>
<p>Are they choleric, sanguine, phlegmatic or melancholic? Are they shy, outgoing?</p>
<p>What is the outcome? How do the characters change because of it? Does the FBI fail to contain this due to ignorance, hubris, bad luck or do they succeed? Do our agents' character flaws lead to that failure or do they prevail in spite of them?</p>

							</div>

								
					
